{"type":"text","timestamp":1794306952168,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"id":"prt_1c5074bd70017qGjWD44dwh1ek","messageID":"msg_1c50738cb001UFFcw8lZNd1fdM","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","type":"text","text":"<think>The failures are due to my setUp deleting all reports (which removes the seeded ones). The seed only happens on first start. My test setUp wipes the reports, so subsequent tests see an empty store.\n\nI should make setUp re-seed after clearing, or not delete the reports in setUp (instead create fresh data per test). Let me change setUp to delete reports and then re-seed the sample reports (call store.seed_sample_reports after clearing the meta flag... but seed_sample_reports returns early if the meta flag exists).\n\nSimplest: in setUp, after deleting reports, insert the sample reports directly. Let me add a helper in the test to re-seed: delete the meta 'seeded' key and call store.seed_sample_reports(conn).\n\nLet me update setUp:\n```python\nself.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM reports\")\nself.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM meta WHERE key='seeded'\")\nstore.seed_sample_reports(self.conn)\n```\n\nThat restores the 6 sample reports per test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794306952151,"end":1794306952165}}}
