{"type":"text","timestamp":1794306977135,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"id":"prt_1c507ad57001siSoAz570tqmNU","messageID":"msg_1c507a000001EKwsUr1njIVFrO","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","type":"text","text":"<think>All backend tests pass. Now let me double check a couple of edge behaviors:\n\n1. `GET /api/weather?city=` (empty) → no filter, no lookup. ✓ (city.strip() → \"\" → falsy)\n2. `GET /api/weather/recent` route ordering vs `/api/weather/<int:report_id>` ✓\n3. The catch-all route for /api paths ✓\n\nLet me now write the frontend. First set up Tailwind.\n\npackage.json: add devDependencies \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.3.5\", \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.3.5\". Then vite.config.ts adds the plugin. Then src/index.css with `@import \"tailwindcss\";`.\n\nLet me run npm install to update package-lock.json.\n\nNote the Dockerfile uses `npm ci` when package-lock.json exists — so the lock must be in sync with package.json. `npm install` updates it.\n\nLet's do it.</think>\n\nBackend works. Now the frontend setup with Tailwind:","time":{"start":1794306977111,"end":1794306977131}}}
