{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794307468961,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"id":"prt_1c50f2e7f001A3SFr55rUYUlxr","messageID":"msg_1c50f04160012psJoqRRPHhxzD","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794307468962,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"id":"prt_1c50f2e81001AlHoXHG1eTKZSK","messageID":"msg_1c50f04160012psJoqRRPHhxzD","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the setup file and the tests. The setup file imports @testing-library/jest-dom and stubs localStorage cleanup.\n\nThe test will mock `fetch` to route to the real Flask server running at http://127.0.0.1:8000? That requires the server to be running during the test — fragile for a committed test. Better: mock fetch with an in-memory fake API implementing the endpoints. That tests the UI logic thoroughly and deterministically.\n\nLet me write a fake fetch that handles:\n- GET /api/weather?city=... \n- GET /api/weather/recent?limit=5\n- POST /api/auth/register, /api/auth/login\n- GET /api/auth/me\n- POST /api/auth/logout\n- POST/PUT/DELETE /api/weather\n- GET /api/weather (list)\n\nI'll implement a small in-memory server in the test file.\n\nThis is a decent amount of code but valuable to verify the React app works (search → card, unit toggle, sign-in flow, add report with validation errors, delete with confirm).\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```tsx\nimport { beforeEach, afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen, waitFor, within } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport App from \"../App\";\n```\n\nThe fake fetch:\n\n```ts\ntype Report = {...};\n\nfunction createApi() {\n  const reports: Report[] = [\n    { id: 1, city: \"Berlin\", country: \"Germany\", temperature_c: 18, condition: \"Cloudy\", humidity: 72, wind_kph: 15, observed_at: \"2026-01-01T10:00:00Z\" },\n    ...\n  ];\n  const lookups = [];\n  const users = new Map();\n  let nextId = 10;\n  \n  const fetchMock = async (input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => {\n    const url = typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.toString();\n    const method = (init?.method ?? \"GET\").toUpperCase();\n    const body = init?.body ? JSON.parse(init.body as string) : undefined;\n    ...\n    return new Response(JSON.stringify(payload), { status, headers: {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"} });\n  };\n}\n```\n\nResponse is available in Node 24 (undici) and jsdom env? In vitest's jsdom environment, `Response` global might be jsdom's (which lacks fetch Response?). Vitest jsdom environment provides Node globals for fetch? jsdom doesn't implement fetch/Response; vitest's jsdom env copies over some Node globals like fetch? Vitest's jsdom environment does add `fetch`, `Response`, `Request`, `Headers` from Node (it has `populateGlobal` with keys including fetch in newer versions). To be safe, I'll construct a minimal fake response object instead of using the Response class:\n\n```ts\nfunction jsonResponse(payload: unknown, status = 200) {\n  return {\n    ok: status >= 200 && status < 300,\n    status,\n    text: async () => JSON.stringify(payload),\n  } as unknown as Response;\n}\n```\nMy api.ts uses `response.status`, `response.text()`, `response.ok`. And `new Headers(options.headers)` — jsdom provides Headers? jsdom implements Headers (yes, jsdom has Headers? Actually jsdom does NOT implement fetch API including Headers... hmm. jsdom does provide Headers? Let me think: jsdom implements XMLHttpRequest but not fetch. The `Headers` class is not part of jsdom. But vitest's jsdom environment may leave Node's global Headers available since jsdom's window doesn't define it — in vitest, globals from Node (like Headers, fetch) remain accessible in the test environment because vitest populates the global with Node's globals where jsdom lacks them. Vitest's `populateGlobal` keeps existing Node globals that aren't defined by jsdom. Yes — vitest's jsdom env only overrides the keys jsdom provides; other Node globals (fetch, Headers, Response) remain.\n\nTo be safe, in my api.ts I use `new Headers(options.headers)`. If Headers is undefined in the test env, it breaks. Let me avoid the Headers API entirely and use a plain object for headers — simpler and more portable:\n\n```ts\nconst headers: Record<string, string> = {};\nif (options.body !== undefined) headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\nif (token) headers[\"Authorization\"] = `Bearer ${token}`;\nconst response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });\n```\nThat's fine — the HeadersInit type accepts a Record<string,string>. Let me refactor api.ts to avoid `new Headers`.\n\nAlso `window.localStorage` — jsdom provides localStorage. ✓\n\n`window.dispatchEvent(new Event(...))` ✓.\n\n`new Date(value).toLocaleString` ✓.\n\nLet me refactor api.ts to use a plain record for headers.\n\nThen write the test file. Tests:\n\n1. \"shows a weather card for a known city\" — type \"Berlin\" → click Search → expect \"Berlin\" in the card, temperature \"18.0°C\", humidity \"72%\", wind \"15 km/h\".\n2. \"converts to Fahrenheit\" — click °F → expect \"64.4°F\".\n3. \"shows no data message\" — type \"Atlantis\" → \"No weather data for Atlantis\".\n4. \"records lookups and repeats them\" — after a search, the recent list shows the city; click it → search repeats (fetch called again).\n5. \"signs in and shows the account\" — register → signed-in user shows username.\n6. \"adds a report and shows API validation messages\" — submit an empty form → shows \"city is required\".\n7. \"deletes a report after confirmation\" — mock window.confirm → true; click Delete → the report disappears.\n\nThat's a good suite. Let me write it.\n\nFor the confirm: `vi.spyOn(window, \"confirm\").mockReturnValue(true)`.\n\nLet me write the test file at frontend/src/__tests__/App.test.tsx, and the setup at frontend/src/test/setup.ts.\n\nNote the tsconfig includes \"src\" so the test files are typechecked. `types: [\"vitest/globals\", ...]` gives globals. But I'll import explicitly from vitest anyway.\n\nAlso @testing-library/jest-dom matchers need the setup file: `import \"@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\";`.\n\nLet me write.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794307468929,"end":1794307468947}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794307468962,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c50f28e875af8fca4b9f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts","newString":"async function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = {};\n  if (options.body !== undefined) {\n    headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n  }\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) {\n    headers[\"Authorization\"] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n  }\n\n  const response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });","oldString":"async function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers = new Headers(options.headers);\n  if (options.body !== undefined) {\n    headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n  }\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) {\n    headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n  }\n\n  const response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n@@ -56,15 +56,15 @@\n   }\n }\n \n async function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n-  const headers = new Headers(options.headers);\n+  const headers: Record<string, string> = {};\n   if (options.body !== undefined) {\n-    headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n+    headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n   }\n   const token = getToken();\n   if (token) {\n-    headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n+    headers[\"Authorization\"] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n   }\n \n   const response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });\n   if (response.status === 204) {\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n@@ -56,15 +56,15 @@\n   }\n }\n \n async function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n-  const headers = new Headers(options.headers);\n+  const headers: Record<string, string> = {};\n   if (options.body !== undefined) {\n-    headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n+    headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n   }\n   const token = getToken();\n   if (token) {\n-    headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n+    headers[\"Authorization\"] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n   }\n \n   const response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });\n   if (response.status === 204) {\n","additions":3,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/api.ts","time":{"start":1794307468936,"end":1794307468959}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c50f2e83001oAEBvTtwQMtuar","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","messageID":"msg_1c50f04160012psJoqRRPHhxzD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794307468999,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c50f2c5b7058813aa8f0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import \"@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\";\nimport { cleanup } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { afterEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nafterEach(() => {\n  cleanup();\n  window.localStorage.clear();\n});\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/test/setup.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/test/setup.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/test/setup.ts","time":{"start":1794307468944,"end":1794307468981}},"id":"prt_1c50f2e8b0013gXd03yOVgj01b","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","messageID":"msg_1c50f04160012psJoqRRPHhxzD"}}
