{"type":"text","timestamp":1794307497629,"sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","part":{"id":"prt_1c50f9e6b001A5gAwjor3BPGVA","messageID":"msg_1c50f831700155g4ABBNf47Twb","sessionID":"ses_e3afb8e6dffemZh34YunfKALwC","type":"text","text":"<think>6 of 7 pass. The failing one: \"adds a report and shows the validation message from the api\" — after clicking \"Add report\" with an empty form, the expected \"city is required\" message isn't found.\n\nWhy? Because clicking \"Add report\" with an empty city → the fake API returns 400 with errors {city: \"city is required\"}. The ReportForm catches ApiError and sets errors. But wait — the form's submit button is labeled \"Add report\" and the title heading is also \"Add a report\". `screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add report\" })` — the heading is \"Add a report\" (an h3, not a button). OK.\n\nHmm, but the issue might be that the form validation errors are rendered... Let me check: in ReportForm, `errors` state is set from error.errors. The Field component renders `errors.city` under the city input. But wait — in the ReportsPanel, `handleCreate` throws → ReportForm catches → sets errors. Should work.\n\nUnless... the click didn't submit the form. Let me look at the error output more closely — the dump shows the ReportsPanel rendered. The failure is at findByText(\"city is required\").\n\nPossibility: the form's `<button type=\"submit\">` is inside the form ✓. Clicking should submit. But `userEvent.click` on a submit button inside a form with `noValidate` → submits → handleSubmit runs.\n\nHmm, but maybe the request failed differently: my fake API's POST branch checks `missingCity` → returns 400 with `{error: ..., errors: {city: \"city is required\"}}`. Then api.ts throws ApiError with errors → ReportForm sets errors → the Field for \"city\" shows it.\n\nWait — the Field id is \"city\" and label \"City\" — the error paragraph renders \"city is required\". Should be found...\n\nUnless the form's City field id collides with the AuthPanel's? No, the auth panel is replaced by ReportsPanel when signed in.\n\nHmm, maybe the click on \"Add report\" didn't happen because there are two elements matching the button name \"Add report\"? getByRole would throw if multiple. It didn't throw, so only one.\n\nLet me debug by printing the actual DOM. Maybe the error message is rendered but with different text: In my fake API, `Object.values(errors)[0]` = \"city is required\" ✓.\n\nWait... maybe the issue is that clicking the button happened before React attached? No.\n\nHmm, maybe the problem: `await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add report\" }))` — the accessible name of the submit button is \"Add report\" ✓.\n\nLet me actually check whether the API call was made. Possibly `handleCreate` threw a non-ApiError (e.g., a JSON parse error) and the message shown was \"Could not reach the server...\". Let me run just that test with more output.\n\nActually! I see it: in `installFakeApi`, the POST branch is inside `if (url.startsWith(\"/api/weather\"))` — but the check `if (method === \"GET\" && city !== null)` etc. For POST, `parsed.searchParams.get(\"city\")` is null → falls through to `if (method === \"GET\")` → false → then `if (method === \"POST\" || method === \"PUT\")` ✓. OK.\n\nHmm wait, there's an earlier branch: `if (url.startsWith(\"/api/weather/recent\"))` — no.\n\nLet me look at the actual rendered output from the failure dump — it was truncated. Let me rerun that single test with a debug print of the form area.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794307497581,"end":1794307497619}}}
